iptionSummary":"In this AWS re:Invent session from 2018, learn how the cloud network engineering team at Netflix automates and manages an infrastructure that services over 125 million customers using Amazon Route 53 and Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud (Amazon EC2).","imageSrcUrl":"https://d1.awsstatic.com/Customer%20References%20Directory%20Logos/Netflix_1x.4ae5e442fea7c25ec27b81891425de0b830cbfcc.png","displayLocation":"United States","customerNameLower":"netflix","footerInfoText":"Published Date","industry":"Media \u0026 Entertainment","sortDate":"2018-01-01","headlineUrl":"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/case-studies/netflix-reinvent-2018-day-in-the-life-of-a-cloud-network-engineer-at-netflix/?did\u003dcr_card\u0026trk\u003dcr_card","customer-name":"Netflix","publishedDate":"2018","enableShare":"1","headline":"Another Day in the Life of a Cloud Network Engineer at Netflix","contentType":"Customer Story"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#product#ec2","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"Amazon EC2","description":"Amazon EC2","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:02:51+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:31+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#customer-story","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Customer Story","description":"Customer Story","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:24+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:07+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#location#namer","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#location","name":"North America","description":"North America","dateCreated":"2020-02-03T05:29:03+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:34+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#tech-category#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#tech-category","name":"Compute","description":"Compute","dateCreated":"2020-01-16T17:43:11+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:35:23+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#location#united-states","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#location","name":"United States","description":"United States","dateCreated":"2020-02-03T05:29:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:34+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#customer-segment#enterprise","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#customer-segment","name":"Enterprise (ENT)","description":"Enterprise (ENT)","dateCreated":"2021-06-04T06:35:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:14+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#language#english","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#language","name":"English","description":"English","dateCreated":"2020-03-03T06:40:42+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:23+0000"},{"id":"customer-references#innovator#netflix","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"customer-references#innovator","name":"Netflix","description":"Netflix","dateCreated":"2022-04-25T19:06:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-06-10T21:39:50+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#product#route53","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"Amazon Route 53","description":"Amazon Route 53","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:05:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:58+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#location#americas","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#location","name":"Americas","description":"Americas","dateCreated":"2020-02-03T05:29:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:29+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#video","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Video","description":"Video","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:43+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:11+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#industry#media-entertainment","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#industry","name":"Media \u0026 Entertainment","description":"Media \u0026 Entertainment","dateCreated":"2020-01-16T17:42:34+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:07+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#tech-category#networking-content-dev","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#tech-category","name":"Networking \u0026 Content Delivery","description":"Networking \u0026 Content Delivery","dateCreated":"2020-01-16T17:43:28+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:35:29+0000"},{"id":"customer-references#customer-segment#enterprise","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"customer-references#customer-segment","name":"Enterprise","description":"Enterprise","dateCreated":"2019-07-22T18:39:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-05T01:27:39+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"customer-references#heartflow-case-study","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"customer-references","name":"heartflow-case-study","dateCreated":"2019-07-19T15:12:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-07-12T01:35:34+0000","additionalFields":{"featured":"0","descriptionSummary":"HeartFlow is a medical technology company that is transforming how heart disease is diagnosed and treated. HeartFlow uses a SaaS model to receive computed tomography data, then applies deep learning to create a digital 3D model of the heart.","imageSrcUrl":"https://d1.awsstatic.com/Customer%20References%20Directory%20Logos/HeartFlow_Customer-Reference__Logo.aa42899df85e35663a639a06e7727aa111b4171b.png","displayLocation":"Americas","footerInfoText":"Published Date","description":"\u003cp\u003eHeartFlow is a medical technology company that is transforming how heart disease is diagnosed and treated. HeartFlow uses a SaaS model to receive computed tomography data, then applies deep learning to create a digital 3D model of the heart. As the company looked to scale globally, HeartFlow transitioned its first-of-its-kind technology to AWS, enabling more frequent software updates and improved uptime. The company uses Amazon S3 to store the data the platform ingests and generates, Amazon EC2 to perform advanced modeling, and Amazon Aurora to track segregated patient data.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","industry":"Life Sciences","sortDate":"2018-01-01","headlineUrl":"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/case-studies/HeartFlow/?did\u003dcr_card\u0026trk\u003dcr_card","customer-name":"HeartFlow","enableShare":"1","publishedDate":"2018","contentType":"Customer Story","headline":"HeartFlow Case Study"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#language#english","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#language","name":"English","description":"English","dateCreated":"2020-03-03T06:40:42+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:23+0000"},{"id":"customer-references#category#high-performance-computing","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"customer-references#category","name":"High Performance Computing","description":"High Performance Computing","dateCreated":"2019-07-22T18:32:00+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-26T01:35:03+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#tech-category#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#tech-category","name":"Compute","description":"Compute","dateCreated":"2020-01-16T17:43:11+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:35:23+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#tech-category#databases","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#tech-category","name":"Databases","description":"Databases","dateCreated":"2020-01-16T17:43:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:35:27+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#location#americas","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#location","name":"Americas","description":"Americas","dateCreated":"2020-02-03T05:29:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:29+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#customer-story","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Customer Story","description":"Customer Story","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:24+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:07+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#product#elasticache","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"Amazon ElastiCache","description":"Amazon ElastiCache","dateCreated":"2020-03-03T00:13:21+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:33+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#case-study","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Case Study","description":"Case Study","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:20+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:07+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#product#ec2","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"Amazon EC2","description":"Amazon EC2","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:02:51+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:31+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#industry#life-sciences","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#industry","name":"Life Sciences","description":"Life Sciences","dateCreated":"2020-01-16T17:42:31+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:06+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#product#s3","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"Amazon Simple Storage Service (S3)","description":"Amazon Simple Storage Service (S3)","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:05:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:58+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#tech-category#serverless","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#tech-category","name":"Serverless","description":"Serverless","dateCreated":"2021-07-28T18:46:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:35:33+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#product#aurora","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"Amazon Aurora","description":"Amazon Aurora","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:01:37+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:18+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#use-case#high-perform-compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#use-case","name":"High Performance Compute","description":"High Performance Compute","dateCreated":"2020-06-05T06:37:26+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:35:41+0000"},{"id":"customer-references#category#databases","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"customer-references#category","name":"Databases","description":"Databases","dateCreated":"2019-07-22T18:31:42+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-12T02:01:30+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#tech-category#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#tech-category","name":"Storage","description":"Storage","dateCreated":"2020-01-16T17:43:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:35:33+0000"},{"id":"customer-references#industry#healthcare-lifesciences","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"customer-references#industry","name":"healthcare-lifesciences","description":"\u003cp\u003eThis tag is initially being created specifically for the Directory Cards componenet on aws.amazon.com/health/case-studies/. When the GCRP decided to add multilingual content to the CSDIR in 2023, the owners of this page only wanted to display the English content in our Directory. Because the Directory Cards component on their page uses an OR operator to pull in content from two tags, they would be unable to add a prefilter condition to look for only English content. This can only be done if the page is using an AND operator. Thus, this tag will be autoapplied to all content that meets the current prefilter conditions. At that point, the page owners can use the AND operator to display content with this tag and GLOBAL#language#english.\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2023-04-26T20:23:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-04-26T20:23:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"customer-references#skyscanner-support","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"customer-references","name":"skyscanner-support","dateCreated":"2020-06-08T17:47:34+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-07-14T23:32:31+0000","additionalFields":{"descriptionSummary":"Skyscanner uses AWS to completely operate its IT infrastructure in the cloud. AWS Support helps Skyscanner to ensure it has the right balance for its large volume of Amazon Enterprise Compute Cloud (EC2) instances to make sure its business is optimized for both performance and cost.","imageSrcUrl":"https://d1.awsstatic.com/Customer%20References%20Directory%20Logos/Skyscanner_Logo@1x.7a44b6e57d8fce63df63a2eff5a60f2cda095fd9.png","displayLocation":"Europe, Middle East, \u0026 Africa","footerInfoText":"Published Date","industry":"Travel \u0026 Hospitality","sortDate":"2018-01-01","headlineUrl":"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/case-studies/skyscanner-support?did\u003dcr_card\u0026trk\u003dcr_card","enableShare":"1","publishedDate":"2018","customer-name":"Skyscanner","contentType":"Customer Story","headline":"Skyscanner support case study"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#industry#hospitality","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#industry","name":"Hospitality","description":"Hospitality","dateCreated":"2020-01-16T17:42:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:05+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#language#english","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#langua