 their page uses an OR operator to pull in content from two tags, they would be unable to add a prefilter condition to look for only English content. This can only be done if the page is using an AND operator. Thus, this tag will be autoapplied to all content that meets the current prefilter conditions. At that point, the page owners can use the AND operator to display content with this tag and GLOBAL#language#english.\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2023-04-26T20:23:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-04-26T20:23:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"customer-references#aws-case-study-penn-state","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"customer-references","name":"aws-case-study-penn-state","dateCreated":"2019-07-22T19:57:53+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-07-12T01:35:33+0000","additionalFields":{"featured":"0","descriptionSummary":"Penn State\u0027s Biological Engineering Department wanted to make its research results widely available to scientists. By using AWS, Penn State has allowed researchers to design more than 50,000 synthetic DNA sequences.","imageSrcUrl":"https://d1.awsstatic.com/logos/600x400_logos/600x400_PennState_Logo.551c1112f3446244428f27923d1f683f9783f3d7.png","displayLocation":"United States","footerInfoText":"Published Date","description":"\u003cp\u003ePenn State?s Biological Engineering Department wanted to make its research results widely available to scientists. Penn State uses AWS to host and distribute its research design methods, optimization algorithms, and results with 6,000 scientists all over the world. By using AWS, Penn State has allowed researchers to design more than 50,000 synthetic DNA sequences.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","industry":"Education","sortDate":"2014-01-01","headlineUrl":"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/case-studies/penn-state/?did\u003dcr_card\u0026trk\u003dcr_card","customer-name":"Penn State","enableShare":"1","publishedDate":"2014","contentType":"Customer Story","headline":"AWS Case Study: Penn State"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#video","locale"